HST PDF: say why signing failed - token or key not found, PIN cancelled, wrong PIN - and log it.

Every signing failure showed one message, "check that the USB token is plugged in and the PIN is
correct", even when token and PIN were fine; release builds have no SAL_LOG, so nothing told what
failed. The Windows signer (svl, hst-windows-csp-token-keys.patch) now records the failing step
and its Windows error code (svl::crypto::GetLastSigningError). After a failed signature the viewer
shows the matching message - token or private key not found, PIN prompt cancelled, wrong or
blocked PIN, or the general message - with "Technical details: <step> 0x<code>" as secondary text,
and appends an entry to the HST log (<profile>/user/hst-office/hst-office.log, the file the Python
components write, same format): "<UTC> ERROR pdf-sign: signing failed: <kind> at <step> 0x<code>".
Only the step and code are logged: no names, paths or PINs. Other platforms record nothing and
keep the general message.

License: MPL-2.0 (modified LibreOffice files keep their license).
Test: needs a Windows build and a token; the strings and the log entry are not covered by a unit test.
